# Publication font settings

This chapter owns `src/publication-settings.ts` and its headless tests. It reads
only root `index.literate` SETTINGS tokens from a `ParsedProject`; `parseProject`
has already canonicalized paths with `safeRelativePath`. Chapter settings and
unrelated keys (including theme) are not ours. Keys and `on`/`off` are case-sensitive.

Code defaults to Lilex Nerd Font, whose regular, bold, italic and bold-italic
files all report that exact family via `fc-scan`. Native italic faces avoid
requiring synthesis for the default code comments.

This is font selection, **not font bundling**. There is no filesystem access,
font lookup, global installation, or runtime dependency. Renderers remain
responsible for applying the selected families and ligature policy. In particular,
`off` calls for disabling `calt` (`-calt`), verified for the actual D2 font, rather
than merely disabling `liga`. This chapter does not change a renderer or CLI.


## Public contract

All five families are resolved strings. Omitted notes inherit the final selected
body family, whereas fragments default independently to Monofur. Diagnostics
here describe settings only: they do not copy `project.diagnostics`. Callers must
still gate rendering on source diagnostics through preparation (`preparePandoc`);
a settings result alone is not permission to render. Source NUL rejection belongs
to the existing parser, before Markdown can replace NUL with a replacement glyph.

```ts : <<publication settings contract>>=
import type { GenerationDiagnostic, ParsedProject } from './engine';

export interface PublicationFonts {
    body: string;
    heading: string;
    code: string;
    fragment: string;
    note: string;
}
export interface PublicationSettingsResult {
    fonts: PublicationFonts;
    codeLigatures: boolean;
    diagnostics: GenerationDiagnostic[];
}
```

## Scan in authored order

Each call starts fresh. A missing root is valid and yields defaults. We consume
the existing fence tokens, including fences inside Markdown containers, without
reparsing source or treating ordinary code blocks as settings.

```ts : <<publication settings resolver>>=
export function resolvePublicationSettings(project: ParsedProject): PublicationSettingsResult {
    const fonts: PublicationFonts = {
        body: 'Latin Modern Roman', heading: 'Monofur Nerd Font',
        code: 'Lilex Nerd Font', fragment: 'Monofur Nerd Font', note: ''
    };
    let codeLigatures = true;
    let explicitNote = false;
    const diagnostics: GenerationDiagnostic[] = [];
    const document = project.documents.find(value => value.path === 'index.literate');
    for (const token of document?.tokens ?? []) {
        if (token.type !== 'fence' || token.info.trim() !== 'SETTINGS') { continue; }
        token.content.split('\n').forEach((line: string, index: number) => {
            const match = /^\s*(font-body|font-heading|font-code|font-fragment|font-note|font-code-ligatures)\s*=(.*)$/.exec(line);
            if (!match) { return; }
            const key = match[1];
            const value = match[2].trim();
```

Family values use the same simple ASCII grammar as the existing LaTeX `fontName`:
1–100 letters, digits, spaces, dots or hyphens, starting with a letter or digit.
Whitespace around values is trimmed; empty names, paths and TeX syntax are rejected.
Last valid wins, but every invalid occurrence remains a diagnostic, just as for
theme settings. Coordinates are zero-based: the fence map starts at its opener,
so content line zero is source line `map[0] + 1`, also within lists and quotes.

```ts : <<publication settings resolver>>=+
            const report = (message: string): void => {
                diagnostics.push({ path: document!.path,
                    line: (token.map?.[0] ?? 0) + index + 1, column: 0, message });
            };
            if (key === 'font-code-ligatures') {
                if (value === 'on' || value === 'off') { codeLigatures = value === 'on'; }
                else { report(`Invalid ${key}: expected on or off`); }
            } else if (/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 .-]{0,99}$/.test(value)) {
                const role = key.slice(5) as keyof PublicationFonts;
                fonts[role] = value;
                if (role === 'note') { explicitNote = true; }
            } else {
                report(`Invalid ${key}: font must be a simple family name (1–100 ASCII characters)`);
            }
        });
    }
    if (!explicitNote) { fonts.note = fonts.body; }
    return { fonts, codeLigatures, diagnostics };
}
```

## Headless contract tests

The contract tests parse real Markdown rather than constructing tokens. They cover
root normalization, containers, newline maps, and invalid-value retention. Neither
resolving settings nor testing them requires an installed font.

The helper rejects unexpected parse diagnostics so settings validation is tested
independently of source validation.

```ts : <<publication settings test setup>>=
import assert = require('node:assert/strict');
import { test } from 'node:test';
import { parseProject } from '../../engine';
import { preparePandoc } from '../../publication-pandoc';
import { resolvePublicationSettings } from '../../publication-settings';
import type { PublicationFonts, PublicationSettingsResult } from '../../publication-settings';

const defaults: PublicationFonts = {
    body: 'Latin Modern Roman', heading: 'Monofur Nerd Font',
    code: 'Lilex Nerd Font', fragment: 'Monofur Nerd Font', note: 'Latin Modern Roman'
};
const fence = (content: string, info = 'SETTINGS') => '```' + info + '\n' + content + '\n```\n';
function resolve(text: string, path = 'index.literate'): PublicationSettingsResult {
    const project = parseProject([{ path, text }]);
    assert.deepEqual(project.diagnostics, []);
    return resolvePublicationSettings(project);
}
```

Defaults are per-call values, and only the canonical, exact-case root participates.
A chapter named `index.literate` is still not the root.

```ts : <<publication settings default tests>>=
test('publication settings defaults and root-only scope', () => {
    const expected = { fonts: defaults, codeLigatures: true, diagnostics: [] };
    assert.deepEqual(resolvePublicationSettings(parseProject([])), expected);
    assert.deepEqual(resolve(''), expected);
    for (const path of ['chapter.literate', 'chapters/index.literate', 'Index.literate']) {
        assert.deepEqual(resolve(fence('font-body=Other\nfont-code-ligatures=bad'), path), expected);
    }
    const project = parseProject([
        { path: 'chapter.literate', text: fence('font-body=Chapter\nfont-note=') },
        { path: './parts/../index.literate', text: fence('font-body=Root') }
    ]);
    assert.deepEqual(project.diagnostics, []);
    assert.equal(resolvePublicationSettings(project).fonts.body, 'Root');
    assert.deepEqual(resolvePublicationSettings(project).diagnostics, []);
    const rejected = parseProject([{ path: '.\\index.literate', text: fence('font-body=Wrong') }]);
    assert.ok(rejected.diagnostics.some(d => d.message === 'Invalid source path'));
    assert.deepEqual(resolvePublicationSettings(rejected), expected);
    const changed = resolve('');
    changed.fonts.body = 'Changed';
    assert.deepEqual(resolve(''), expected);
});
```

Every role accepts trimmed names. Note inheritance is delayed across SETTINGS
blocks, but an explicit valid note survives subsequent invalid note values.

```ts : <<publication settings default tests>>=+
test('publication settings select all roles and delay note inheritance', () => {
    const result = resolve(fence('font-body = Body 2.0\nfont-heading= Heading-Font \n' +
        'font-code= Code Font \nfont-fragment= Fragment Font\nfont-code-ligatures= off '));
    assert.deepEqual(result, { fonts: { body: 'Body 2.0', heading: 'Heading-Font',
        code: 'Code Font', fragment: 'Fragment Font', note: 'Body 2.0' },
        codeLigatures: false, diagnostics: [] });
    const inherited = resolve(fence('font-note=\nfont-body=First') + fence('font-body=Last'));
    assert.equal(inherited.fonts.note, 'Last');
    assert.equal(inherited.diagnostics.length, 1);
    const explicit = resolve(fence('font-note=Notes') + fence('font-body=Last\nfont-note=bad/path'));
    assert.equal(explicit.fonts.note, 'Notes');
    assert.equal(explicit.diagnostics.length, 1);
});
```

Invalid repetitions never erase a valid value or an earlier diagnostic. Valid
ligature values likewise override only the selected value, not diagnostic history.

```ts : <<publication settings validation tests>>=
test('publication settings retain every invalid repetition', () => {
    const result = resolve(fence('font-body=\nfont-body=First\nfont-body=bad/path\n' +
        'font-body=Last\nfont-body=\\input{x}\nfont-code-ligatures=no\n' +
        'font-code-ligatures=off\nfont-code-ligatures=ON') +
        fence('font-code-ligatures=on\nfont-code-ligatures='));
    assert.equal(result.fonts.body, 'Last');
    assert.equal(result.fonts.note, 'Last');
    assert.equal(result.codeLigatures, true);
    assert.deepEqual(result.diagnostics.map(d => d.line), [1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 12]);
    assert.ok(result.diagnostics.every(d => d.path === 'index.literate' && d.column === 0));
    assert.match(result.diagnostics[0].message, /font-body.*simple family name/);
    assert.match(result.diagnostics[3].message, /font-code-ligatures.*on or off/);
});
```

The grammar is deliberately narrower than fontspec input; no TeX escaping or path
interpretation is attempted. All five family keys share this validation.

```ts : <<publication settings validation tests>>=+
test('publication settings enforce the simple ASCII family grammar', () => {
    const invalid = ['', '   ', 'A'.repeat(101), '.Font', '-Font', 'École', 'A_B',
        'A/B', 'A\\B', 'A{B}', 'A%B', 'A#B', 'A$B', 'A&B', 'A~B', 'A^B', 'A[B]', 'A\tB'];
    for (const role of ['body', 'heading', 'code', 'fragment', 'note'] as const) {
        for (const value of invalid) {
            const result = resolve(fence('font-' + role + '=' + value));
            assert.equal(result.fonts[role], defaults[role], role + ': ' + value);
            assert.equal(result.diagnostics.length, 1, role + ': ' + value);
        }
        for (const value of ['A', '0', 'A'.repeat(100), 'Family 2.0-Pro']) {
            const result = resolve(fence('font-' + role + '=  ' + value + '  '));
            assert.equal(result.fonts[role], value);
            assert.deepEqual(result.diagnostics, []);
        }
    }
});
```

Unrelated SETTINGS and non-SETTINGS text are ignored, including differently cased
keys, ordinary fences and indented code. Container fences remain ordinary settings.

```ts : <<publication settings source tests>>=
test('publication settings ignore unrelated keys and non-settings text', () => {
    const text = fence('theme=unknown\nFont-body=\nfont-body-extra=\nfont-note-other=\nauthors=X') +
        fence('font-body=Wrong', 'settings') + fence('font-body=Wrong', 'text') +
        'font-body=Wrong\n\n    font-body=Wrong\n';
    assert.deepEqual(resolve(text), { fonts: defaults, codeLigatures: true, diagnostics: [] });
});

test('publication settings map zero-based lines across newlines and containers', () => {
    const lines = ['# Title', '', '> ```SETTINGS', '> font-body=Quoted', '> font-heading=',
        '> ```', '', '- item', '', '  ```SETTINGS', '  font-code-ligatures=off',
        '  font-note=bad/path', '  ```'];
    for (const newline of ['\n', '\r\n', '\r']) {
        const result = resolve(lines.join(newline));
        assert.equal(result.fonts.body, 'Quoted');
        assert.equal(result.fonts.note, 'Quoted');
        assert.equal(result.codeLigatures, false);
        assert.deepEqual(result.diagnostics.map(d => [d.line, d.column]), [[4, 0], [11, 0]]);
    }
    assert.equal(resolve(fence('font-body=')).diagnostics[0].line, 1);
});
```

Source diagnostics remain owned by the parser and the preparation gate. Resolving
settings neither duplicates nor mutates them, even when a rejected source is NUL-bearing.

```ts : <<publication settings source tests>>=+
test('publication settings leave source diagnostics to the preparation gate', () => {
    const project = parseProject([{ path: 'index.literate', text: fence('font-body=A\0B') }]);
    assert.ok(project.diagnostics.some(d => /NUL/.test(d.message)));
    const before = JSON.stringify(project);
    assert.deepEqual(resolvePublicationSettings(project), {
        fonts: defaults, codeLigatures: true, diagnostics: []
    });
    const prepared = preparePandoc(project, () => { throw new Error('must not render'); });
    assert.equal(prepared.document, undefined);
    assert.deepEqual(prepared.diagnostics, project.diagnostics);
    assert.equal(JSON.stringify(project), before);
});
```
